<title>USA: AMEX files complaints vs VISA in 5 countries.</title>
<headline>AMEX files complaints vs VISA in 5 countries.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Express Co said Tuesday it is filing legal complaints against Visa in Argentina, Brazil, Colombia and Mexico charging Visa with anti-competitive activities.</p>
<p>The company said it has also asked anti-trust authorities in Puerto Rico to investigate and take appropriate action against Visa.  </p>
<p>American Express said its complaints assert that Visa has imposed a rule limiting competition between American Express and other card systems by restricting the products member banks can offer customers.</p>
<p>The company said the Latin America Regional Board of Visa is adopt and act on the new bylaw next month.</p>
<p>&quot;The bylaw would deny banks the ability to offer their customers a choice of a bank-issued American Express Card, a Visa card, or both,&quot; American Express stated.</p>
</text>
